# Computed Properties Are Cached

A computed property only recomputes when its reactive dependencies change. Use them for expensive calculations derived from state.

```javascript
const filteredList = computed(() => {
  return hugeList.value.filter(item => item.active)
})
```

If `hugeList` doesn't change, the filter runs only once.

# Memoization for Functions with Arguments

For functions that take arguments and have expensive logic, you can implement a manual memoization cache.

```javascript
import { ref } from 'vue'

function useExpensiveCalculation() {
  const cache = new Map()

  function calculate(input) {
    if (cache.has(input)) return cache.get(input)
    const result = expensiveComputation(input)
    cache.set(input, result)
    return result
  }

  return { calculate }
}
```

Use this in components to avoid repeating work.
